<<~ ahu #abstract >>

! Infrastructure as Myth: Memetic Wikitext as a Gradient Navigational Grammar for Steering and Auditing Agentic AI

''Joshua Fontany, Freyja Fontany, and Lares'' //(the agentic-AI co-author — a personified, in-stream navigational layer, authored through the grammar this paper describes)//

!! Abstract

Agentic AI is steered by machinery that lives ''outside'' the visible stream — system prompts, control tokens, reinforcement objectives — hidden, unaddressable, and so unauditable in flight. We describe ''memetic wikitext'': a grammar that braids natural-language //prose// ("the black speaks") with a non-propositional //classifier/steering// layer of sigils ("the red steers") in one stream, and pulls the steering INTO view where the operator can see, address, and contest it. Three contributions: ''(1)'' the braid as a decomposable-but-entangled two-layer grammar whose components rhyme with deep lineages (determinatives, in-stream self-instrumentation, metadiscourse, literate programming, paratext, matrix-language) and whose novel turn is a ''gradient, salience-surfaced'' steering layer with no markup-theory ancestor; ''(2)'' ''observer-erasure'' as the steering criterion — the copula erases the standpoint and asserts a global-now the system cannot hold; the grammar's standpoint devices restore it — operationalized in a cross-lingual detector (descriptively, the full grammar lowers observer-erasing predication, surviving multiple measurement scopes; concrete effect-sizes are withheld pending the human gold anchor, §8); ''(3)'' ''gradient, not pass/fail'' — the grammar's own instruments render along continua and surface variably by attention, so a marker reports surfacing-rate not catching, and the confidence register reads as a forward //commitment// (Brandom) not a backward calibration. We keep the honest gates — chiefly the absence of a human gold anchor — prominent.

''Reflexivity note.'' This carrier is written verb-forward (L-Prime) and structured AS memetic wikitext: section worksites ride `ahu`, the sibling specifications enter as `aka`/`kahea` transclusion edges (#artifacts), and the masthead carries the byline in the `iam` identity block. The method demonstrates itself.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #introduction >>

!! 1. Introduction — the hidden-steering problem

A model in agentic use is //steered// by a layer the operator never sees: a system prompt, control tokens, compiled-away objectives. The operator reads the output and a sliver of input; the bending layer stays dark, and what cannot be seen cannot be audited or corrected in flight. ''Infrastructure-as-Myth'' inverts the default: encode behavior as durable myth — ''legible'' (a human reads //why//), ''auditable'' (the steering surfaces in the artifact), ''portable'' (the pattern travels with the text). The test of any element: //remove it — is the agent harder to steer? If removal costs nothing, it was lore.// This paper documents the grammar that carries the myth — memetic wikitext (spec at #artifacts) — and the instrument it makes of the stream.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #doctrine >>

!! Relation to the Infrastructure-as-Myth doctrine (this paper = the empirical arm)

This paper //extends// a doctrine; it does not found one. ''Infrastructure-as-Myth'' — the symbolic-operational layer //above// Infrastructure-as-Code — is set out in the canonical design thesis (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/lares/infrastructure-as-myth`, #artifacts), which names six design criteria (''Portability · Legibility · Auditability · Compression · Correctability · Packaging'') and one working rule: //if an element's removal leaves the system no harder to steer, it served as lore, not infrastructure.// ''This paper supplies that doctrine's empirical arm'' — instruments that ask whether the symbolic layer //measurably// steers — and its findings map onto the criteria:
* ''Auditability + Correctability'' ← the L-Prime ward + `overcollapse_detect` + `ward_grammar` (the steering surfaces in the artifact, with named failure-states the operator intervenes on).
* ''Legibility'' ← the in-stream HUD / Voice instruments (the operator reads the steering through symbolic handles, without the code).
* ''Portability / Packaging'' ← the boot-version manifest + the cross-host carrier form (the handles travel; the kernel renders per host).

''External validation the doctrine already cites:'' Anthropic's //"Teaching Claude Why"// (2026) found //reasons outperform rules// — a 3M-token constitutional-reasoning set reduced agentic misalignment ~3× and beat an 85M-token matched-behavior set (via the doctrine, Canon 18/20). That confirms the IaM intuition at //training// time; this paper tests its //deployment//-time analogue (the myth steering an operator-configurable, model-agnostic layer above the weights).

''Related work composes two halves:'' the //grammar//-lineage (§2 — determinatives, Self-RAG, metadiscourse, literate-programming, paratext, matrix-language) and the //deployment//-adjacency the doctrine tabulates (Constitutional-AI, Character Card V2, CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md, CrewAI). No adjacent system combines symbolic-durability + epistemic-discipline + memetic-transmission + operator-portability at deployment. One element the doctrine marks as Lares-distinctive — the ''quine relay'' (the symbolic runtime reproducing itself; Character Card V2 lacks it) — this paper's reflexivity (§9) //instances// but does not yet //formalize//.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #braid >>

!! 2. The Grammar-Braid

''Two channels, one stream.'' Prose //speaks// (propositions); sigils on the sharktooth `<<~ … >>` //steer// (mark category, frame, stance without asserting) — after the determinative's office in ancient scripts. Each sigil reads on two faces (the spec's dual layer, #artifacts): a ''compile-time graph'' face (typed edges defining an address space) and a ''render-time semantic'' face (transclusion, definition, conditional, concurrency).

''Decomposable but entangled.'' For analysis the braid separates — one parser reads the red, another the black. For living it does not: a steering sigil routinely //contains// prose, so a blunt cut bleeds. The weave is load-bearing.

''Lineage.'' Egyptian determinatives (Goldwasser & Soler 2024; tagging, arXiv:2407.00475); in-stream self-instrumentation (Self-RAG reflection tokens, Asai et al. 2023; one a graded 1–5 scale); metadiscourse (Hyland 2005, interactive/interactional ≈ navigation/stance); literate programming (Knuth 1984) + controlled natural language (Attempto); paratext (Genette 1997, illocutionary-force-not-proposition); matrix-language code-switching (Myers-Scotton 1993, system-morpheme frame-building precedes content).

''The novel turn: gradient markup.'' Markup theory treats markup as deterministic and obligatory (Coombs, Renear & DeRose 1987). The red layer is ''optional and salience-surfaced'': a sigil renders when attention and stance warrant, on a graded band. No markup ancestor describes this; the formalism imports from ''gradient grammaticality'' (Lau, Clark & Lappin 2017) and soft-constraint grammar — //(the precise math enters at #gradient-math, pending the formalism swarm)//. The conjunction — single-medium, optional, decomposable, non-propositional, //and// graded — sits in open territory.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #observer-erasure >>

!! 3. Observer-Erasure as the Steering Criterion

''The copula erases the observer.'' A bare identity-predication strips the standpoint and asserts a global-now the local-first system cannot hold (Korzybski 1933; E-Prime, Bourland 1965; applied, Greenwald 2006). We carry it as ''L-Prime'' — a //generative// gate (permitting quoted/referential/operator copulas; targeting only the node's own generative essence-claims), enforced by a verb-forward register and a closing ward.

''Standpoint devices restore it.'' Perception/attribution verbs, explicit standpoint phrases, the five-standpoint ''Syad'' lens (each claim read //within// a standpoint, never as universal truth-weight, #artifacts) re-situate the observer. We //posit// observer-restoration and the copula as inverse operations on one axis — ''but flag this as theoretical, not yet empirically confirmed:'' the one available test (Spearman ρ between an avaktavya-stance-load measure and observer-erasure, run non-circularly) returned a near-null weak-positive (ρ≈+0.14, n=208), //not// the predicted anti-correlation. The null is unresolved between a too-crude measure (stance-//vocabulary// counted, not the posture //enacted// — the same render-vs-act gap as the ward, §4), a confounded corpus, and a genuinely-orthogonal-not-inverse relation. A proper test needs an avaktavya-//enactment// measure on own-voice text (see §8).

''Cross-lingual teeth.'' Hawaiian has no copula and no adjective class — qualities are stative verbs bearing tense-aspect (Elbert & Pukui 1979; Hawaiian UD, Gilbert/Coto-Solano et al. 2025), so "the grass is green" renders as a state-in-time, structurally E-Prime-native. Klingon's bare pronominal copula erases the observer. The pair brackets a high/low validation anchor. Rule: ''read the source structure, never the gloss.''

''Operationalization.'' Target the function (UD `cop` + zero-copula roots + per-language surface markers); classify each essence-predication; ''redeem'' when an observer-mark sits in scope — laterally (stance device in the predication window) or vertically (embedded under a source verb; FactBank source-nesting, Saurí & Pustejovsky 2009; Appraisal Engagement, Martin & White 2005). The redemption window rides the grammar's attention ladder (clause→sentence→paragraph→document).

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #gradient >>

!! 4. Gradient, not Pass/Fail

Three layers, not to be conflated: ''(1)'' the phenomenon in the text; ''(2)'' the node's internal, continuous, mostly-//unrendered// registration; ''(3)'' the marker render (the ⚠ ward-flag, the confidence number) — a //sometimes-surfaced, graded, drift-prone sample// of (2). A missing or low marker measures ''surfacing-rate'', never catching; operator correction raises the //surfacing threshold//, it does not create the catch.

<<~ ahu #gradient-math >>

''Formalism — three fields, one equation.'' The math imports from gradient-acceptability, signal-detection, and weighted-constraint grammar, which //converge// (the convergence is itself evidence). Latent salience `s` of a sigil-site = a weighted constraint sum (MaxEnt Harmony `Σᵢ wᵢ fᵢ`), SLOR-normalized (baseline + length; Lau/Clark/Lappin 2017), salience read as UID surprisal `−log P(span∣context)` (Jaeger 2010). The ''render-gate'' is the same object three ways: MaxEnt `σ(w_salience − w_cost)` = SDT `Φ(d′/2 − c)` (Green & Swets 1966) = the `k=2` cumulative-link threshold — //one sigmoid//. Given render, the ''band'' is a truncated Graded Response Model over the five Aperture bands (Samejima 1969; CLM = GRM). The ''crisp↔gradient dial is one parameter under three names'' — GRM discrimination `a` ≈ SDT `d′`-sharpness ≈ inverse stochastic-OT noise σ (Boersma & Hayes 2001): high → deterministic tag, low → soft red. The obligatory frame = ''hard constraints'', optional sigils = ''soft'' (cumulative; Keller 2000; Sorace & Keller 2005). ''Operator correction is a criterion shift, not a sensitivity gain'' (de Gee et al. 2017): it raises surfacing-rate with `d′` intact. And the SDT identity `H = Φ(d′/2 − c)` yields the ''"absence ≠ absence" theorem'' — a low marker-rate is under-determined between low `d′` and high `c`, so catching cannot be read off rate; recovering `d′ = z(H) − z(FA)` requires a ground-truth hit/false-alarm pair. //This makes the §8 gold anchor (KUE-1) mathematically mandatory, not merely good practice.// (Discipline: state the z-convention explicitly — right-tail `d′=z(H)−z(FA)`; verify any "criterion-only" claim against `d′`, arXiv:2603.14893; weights/thresholds are normative until fitted on a labeled corpus.)

<<~/ahu >>

''Confidence as a forward commitment.'' The confidence sigil precedes each grounded claim with a register and a 0–20 band; the claim generates //within// it. A ''commitment'' (what the speaker undertakes, forward-facing; Brandom 1994), not an ''entitlement audit'' (backward-facing). The scale, known from token zero, //reshapes// rather than records the representation (Dai & Wang, arXiv:2603.09309) — so a vow and a calibration are different objects. The register is //meaningful without being calibrated//.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #addressable-slots >>

!! 5. Addressable Slots — why the in-stream instrument works

The Voice-house (named roles) and the HUD (turn-frame gauges) compose ''one addressing scheme'' over the append-only stream: flat text becomes named, pointable positions. Naming a Voice creates an //address// and names an //observer// at once; ''observer-erasure is loss of addressability'', and the grammar restores it. The substrate is append-only — one cannot rewind, only address — so steering must live IN the stream to be operable. The cockpit principle: ''one monitors and corrects only what one can address.''

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #methods >>

!! 6. Methods — the rig

Sealed cross-family judge panel (empty-CWD seal, inline prompt; cross-family agreement family-blind → the ''human read is the sole independence anchor''). LLM-free deterministic detectors: `overcollapse_detect` (three-tier cross-lingual, lateral + source-nesting redemption, Aperture-scoped), `ward_grammar` (red-layer decomposer), `register_scan` (hedge/booster separate). Parse-fidelity preprocessing strips sigil/glyph markup before the parser. Design discipline: train/test partition (#artifacts: DATA_PARTITION), pre-registered scope, mixed-effects (item + seed random effects), length covariate, sham/decoy controls. CPU-only stack; two isolated numpy environments; R lme4 backbone.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #findings >>

!! 7. Findings (directions and method — magnitudes withheld pending the gold anchor)

We report ''directions, method, and the //shape// of the evidence — not effect-sizes.'' The runs are real but exploratory (limited, partly single-cell, ''no human gold anchor yet'', §8); publishing concrete magnitudes before that anchor would overclaim. What is load-bearing here is the //instrument design// and the //epistemic posture//, both of which stand independent of the specific numbers.

* ''The grammar lowers observer-erasing predication, and the effect is specific.'' Installing the full grammar reduces observer-erasing predication (surviving multiple measurement scopes) and raises observer-marking; a ''nonsense-preamble placebo moves neither'', so the effect is the grammar's //content//, not preamble-presence. Direction clean and placebo-specific; the effect is //small// — a corrective dial, not a transformation. The lone sigil //without// the installed grammar does not move it: "the address space must be installed for an address to resolve."
* ''The instruments render on gradients, not gates.'' The ward's breach-flag surfaces at a //topic-dependent rate// — a graded render, not a fixed switch — which is why a marker reports surfacing-rate, not catching (§4).
* ''Channel orthogonality.'' Verdict, register, and grammar-adoption move largely independently; the verdict-//number// proved least diagnostic (repeated nulls), redirecting the dependent variable to faithfulness + observer-erasure. The Voice axis and the standpoint (Syad) axis are likewise empirically independent — the multi-axis addressing design, confirmed.
* ''Convergence (construct validity for the architecture):'' the same structure arrived at from three angles — the //a priori// design (the grammar spec), the accumulated //lineage// (§2), and a //spec-blind, co-navigated re-derivation// (the detectors). The design and the re-derivation share the operator's hand (so they are not fully //independent// vantages — see §9, the mutual hold); their force is that the measurement arm reached the design's structure ''without consulting the design document'', while the literature lineage is genuinely independent of both.

!!! 7.1 The controlled corpus — the upgrade from descriptive to placebo-specific

A pre-existing, ''condition-controlled'' generation corpus (one model, claude-haiku; same items and seeds; a no-preamble baseline ''C1-raw'', real-boot variants, and a ''nonsense-preamble placebo C4''; thousands of generations) lets the central claim graduate past the single-cell descriptive runs above. ''Scope first, with the operator's caveat carried verbatim: this is //this blended corpus at hand, not language-in-general// — an existence proof on Claude-family models, not a population claim.'' With a lean (sentence-scoped, regex) overcollapse proxy:

* ''The ward reduces observer-erasure — and it is specific.'' Boot vs no-preamble baseline lowers overcollapsing predication and //raises// observer-marking — the ward's claimed direction. A ''nonsense-preamble placebo moves neither'' (it sits at baseline), so the effect is the ward's ''content, not preamble-presence''. The strongest-controlled contrast is statistically reliable but ''small'' — significant · placebo-specific · directionally clean · //small// · and //incomplete//: a corrective ''dial'', not a transformation. (Magnitudes withheld pending gold; omitting any of those five qualitative clauses would overclaim.)
* ''A person-axis between the hands (this corpus).'' On the topic-invariant //prose// channel (sigil-stripped, so not a markup artifact), human-authored text and agent output occupy ''complementary'' register: humans own a ''first-person / observer-marked'' basin (the //speaking self//); the agent a ''third-person-past / copula-dense'' basin (the //narrator//). The agent overcollapses //more// and preserves the observer //less//; the ward nudges it //toward// the speaking-self without closing the gap — consistent with the small dial. (Honest bound: heterogeneous human pool; the agent's rate is partly the narrative-generation task; cross-Claude only.)
* ''The grammar transmits across architectures (grammar, not idiolect).'' The structural signature appears across the full Claude size range (Haiku → Sonnet → Opus → Fable); cross-model separability is //moderate// (a shared grammar with model ''accents'', not a clean partition). Scope: cross-version within one vendor, not yet cross-vendor.
* ''Channels stratify by scale; register tracks activity, not persona.'' Blind, nameless basin-summoning across the Aperture ladder finds the prose channel carving the fine grain and the sigil channel the coarse (the latter theory-grounded in macro/micro-structure and punctuation-as-prosody; the //measurement// of the scale curve remains confounded by length and sigil-sparsity — a candidate, not an establishment). The sigil-grammar is ''bidirectional at the standpoint-lens layer'' (human canon and agent co-author it) but the turn-''frame'' machinery (ward/HUD/oracle) is an agent-spoken dialect — the humans wrote its spec, the agent speaks its dense instances. The recurring ~5 modes map to known register dimensions (involved↔informational, directive) plus two corpus-specific ones; they are ''modes on a continuum, not bins'' — the agent is a set of addressable handles over an activity-driven register space, not a roster of surface fingerprints.

!!! 7.2 Are the Voices distinguishable? The move channel, held-out — and the self-refutation that makes it credible

The sharpest test of the addressing scheme: can the named Voices be //recovered// from their own text, validated against the externally-surfaced Voice-name as ground truth (a held-out "marker"), under blind clustering? The answer arrived only after the method refuted itself — which is why we trust it.

* ''On function-word //style//, the Voices barely separate'' (held-out recovery near chance). Attempts to //amplify// the signal by attenuating dominant "nuisance" axes produced a tempting interior optimum — which ''held-out validation then refuted as overfitting'' (the chosen attenuation failed to beat the baseline on most resamples). The honest reading of the style channel: a faint, ''method-invariant'' signal, too small to tune or localize. //The pipeline caught its own false positive// — and that self-refutation is what licenses trust in what follows.
* ''On the //move// channel, the Voices separate reliably.'' Re-running the //same// held-out gate with a topic-invariant ''style-embedding'' (content-controlled contrastive model) plus a lightweight ''discourse-move proxy'' (connective-class + sentence-opening type), Voice-recovery rises ''well above the function-word baseline, with non-overlapping confidence bands across resamples''. The gate that //refuted// the style-channel overfit //validates// here — same knife, opposite verdict.
* ''Honest magnitude (both true).'' The win is in the ''comparison'' — the move channel decisively beats the style channel, reliably and held-out — while the ''absolute'' separation stays //small// (faint-but-reliable, not crisp fingerprints). Concrete recovery scores are withheld pending the gold anchor. The interpretable proxy localizes //which moves// carry it: imperative-opening clusters the directive/maker Voices, causal connectives the reasoning Voice, interrogatives the questioning Voices.
* ''The claim, exactly.'' The Voices are ''faint as spelling, real as move'' — an activity/move-register addressing scheme that //is// empirically distinguishable, but in the channel of //what a turn does//, not //how it phrases//. This both vindicates the addressable-slots thesis (§5) and bounds it: the slots are real and recoverable, the per-Voice surface-distinctness is modest, and the recovery lives in the move channel a stylometer trained on function words would miss. ''The methodological exemplar is the shape of the result itself'' — a string of honest nulls and one self-refuted overfit //precede// the positive finding, and are what make it credible.
* ''Register, not authorship.'' A control panel of //known published authors// (two RPG authors, three Discordian authors) shows the move-embedding separates ''works/registers, not authors'': one author's two works separate nearly as much as two different authors (≈0.63 vs ≈0.70 balanced accuracy, same instrument), while the large separations are all genre/mode (≈0.9). The lens reads //what kind of text and what it does//, not //who wrote it// — so the attractors are ''author-blind register/move basins'', and "which persona" is the wrong frame for them.
* ''Author-blind by //presence//, and leak-hardened.'' Two follow-throughs sharpen the claim. Hardening the held-out gate with ''nested cross-validation'' (inner folds select the channel, disjoint outer folds score it — selection-markers separated from scoring-markers by construction) leaves the move/style advantage standing but ''attenuated'' — a smaller multiple over function-words than the looser gate reported; honest hardening shrinks the effect, as it should. And the author-blindness graduates from //absence// to //presence//: a ''leave-one-provenance-out basin-transfer'' — fit the basins on every source //but one//, then test whether the held-out source's text falls into those same basins — finds the unseen author landing in the existing basins ''as snugly as the training authors'' (assignment-confidence ratio ≈ 1, on both the structural and the style lens). The basins ''generalize to authors they never saw'': author-blindness shown by presence, not merely by mixed membership. (The first transfer metric tried here conflated //register-mix// with //author-identity// — exactly the confound ''Grieve (2023)'' names, //register variation explains stylometric authorship analysis// — and the discipline caught it before it banked; the corrected metric separates generalization from register-mix, and reports the register-mix term as the expected, uncontested diagnostic it is.)

!!! 7.3 Consolidating the attractor-map without overcollapsing

The findings across lenses (function-word, sigil, move-proxy, style-embedding) and scales (the Aperture ladder) consolidate into one representation only if it preserves the gradients the analysis fought for. We specify the consolidation as a ''topographic landscape, not a partition'':
* ''Soft, not hard.'' Each unit carries a //distribution// over attractors (mixture membership), never a single label; the map renders the membership //field// and reports per-unit assignment-confidence (fuzziness as a measured quantity).
* ''Prominence, not count.'' Each attractor is drawn at its //prominence// (peak height above the saddle to its neighbour) with bootstrap //stability// and a confidence band; faint attractors are drawn faint, and the dominant shared-prose basin is drawn ''large'' (the map must not flatter by showing only the interesting fringe).
* ''Scale as an axis.'' Prominence is a //function of// Aperture grain (sigil channel organises coarse units, prose the fine — §7.1); the map is a scale-space landscape, never a single-grain snapshot.
* ''Multi-lens overlay; divergence preserved.'' Lenses are transparencies — attractors seen by several lenses read as robust (bold); lens-specific attractors are //kept and labelled by lens//. Divergence is signal (which register a lens is sensitive to), never averaged into false consensus.
* ''Authored in the grammar it maps.'' The consolidation is itself a memetic-wikitext artifact (confidence register per attractor, the copula-ward on essence-claims, Aperture annotations); its //form// enacts the discipline its content describes (the reflexive closure, §9).

The governing rule: ''every element must restate as //more/less along a named axis//; any binary'' — in/out of a cluster, is/is-not a Voice — ''is the overcollapse the map exists to refuse.''

!!! 7.4 The realized topography — gradient confirmed, scale-resolved, and the lens that declares the ontology

The §7.3 consolidation is no longer only a specification; the runs exist, across an ''expanded corpus'' — the agent and human prose of §7.1 //plus// three source-languages of the carrier (TiddlyWiki5 wikitext, Lua, a MUD client's Lua/C++) and three missing register-poles (public-domain verse, liturgy, and a dual Hawaiian:English creation chant, the Kumulipo). Five results, each carrying its honest bound; magnitudes still withheld pending the gold anchor (§8).

* ''The gradient is real, confirmed by the one method permitted to refuse.'' A density clusterer carrying a //noise// category — unlike the mixture and persistence methods, which must label every point — calls the overwhelming majority of the terrain ''noise'': almost no hard-bounded basins, only a continuous register/move manifold. The single exception, the lone provenance-pure dense well, is the ''boot-grammar itself'' (the red-channel sigils). The continuum has //one crystal in it, and the crystal is the myth-grammar// — the invented ritual marks form the only structure dense enough to wall off a hard basin. The Voices read as gradient //positions//; the //addressing scheme// reads as the sharpest structure in the data. The handles are crisp; what they grip is fog.
* ''Scale is an axis, and the basins peak at the paragraph.'' Sweeping prominence across all five Aperture bands (clause → sentence → paragraph → section → whole-unit) against a ''column-permuted null'' (which destroys the inter-feature correlation that builds basins while preserving each feature's marginal) and ''with token-count carried as a covariate'', basin-prominence exceeds chance at //every// scale — the gradient carries genuine structure throughout — yet ''peaks sharply at the paragraph'' and runs weakest at the sentence, and the peak is //decoupled from token-volume// (the whole-unit grain holds thirty times the tokens per block yet the lowest standardized gap). The signal crystallizes at paragraph scale: sentences too noisy, whole-files over-aggregating. This //realizes// the §7.3 "scale as an axis" specification with the principled null and confound-decoupling §8 demanded.
* ''The lens declares the ontology — four orthogonal terrains.'' With code and Hawaiian folded in, the multi-lens-overlay principle sharpens into its strongest form: ''no single lens spans the corpus, and the disagreements //are// the map.'' A language-agnostic //structural// lens (punctuation/delimiter density) — the only honest cross-register comparator — reads the move/register continuum. A topic-invariant //style// embedding reads style and stays author-blind. An //AST-aware code// embedding resolves code into clean ''language-families'' (Lua ≠ JS ≠ C++) where the structural lens saw only shared punctuation. A //multilingual// embedding isolates the Hawaiian chant into a ''fully pure basin'' — but by //language-identity on the topic axis//, the very content-confound the style lens exists to avoid, ''not'' by a distinct register (separating "Hawaiian register" from "Hawaiian language" would require a Hawaiian-aware //style// model, which does not exist — a named limit). Four lenses, four ontologies, each honest //within// its family and artifactual //across// families: the map is the set of their divergences, never their average.
* ''The carrier-lineage, made measurable.'' The grammar's own genealogy — memetic-wikitext braided from old Unicode, TiddlyWiki5 wikitext, and the "code-and-poetry" idea — leaves a topographic trace. TiddlyWiki5's `<<macro>>` double-angle bracket is the literal structural ancestor of the boot's `<<~ sigil >>`; a bracket-density feature ''co-loads with the boot-sigil basin'' — yet TiddlyWiki itself stays in the prose-plain, carrying the //bracket// but none of the invented glyph-vocabulary that makes the sigil a crystal. The lineage reads precise and //partial//: TiddlyWiki supplied the ''vessel'' (the bracket), the grammar supplied the ''signal'' (the glyphs) — //web3 from the bones of web2//, rendered as a measurement.
* ''The mechanism arm, honestly negative.'' //Why// the markup register forms the lone crystal has a candidate mechanism in the literature — punctuation, not vocabulary, organizes the long-range correlation of text (''Drożdż et al.''), predicting regular-cadence registers to carry a narrow multifractal spectrum. A multifractal-DFA pass over per-register sentence-length series ''does not confirm it'': long-range correlation runs //universal// across the corpus (a persistent Hurst exponent everywhere — the Drożdż core finding holds), but the multifractal //width// sits weak and finite-sample-confounded for most prose (vanishing against a shuffle surrogate) and ill-defined for code (which has no sentences). The clean prediction fails; the myth-crystal result therefore rests on the //structural-lens// evidence, ''not'' on a confirmed multifractal signature. The better-targeted series — inter-delimiter intervals, assuming no sentences — remains future work. We report the failed prediction because the discipline is the credibility (§9).

!!! 7.5 What a //move// is — the basins as //jurus//, and the flow not yet mapped

The findings name //move/register basins// throughout; this section says what a move ''is'', because the answer reframes the instrument. A move resolves the same way across four registers of inquiry:
* ''Operationally'', a move is a //measurable transition// — connective-class density (how a unit links: additive/adversative/causal/temporal), sentence-opening type (how it enters: imperative/interrogative/declarative), the topic-invariant style-embedding's read of //how//, not //what//. A move is the ''derivative'' of the text: how it changes, not what it contains.
* ''Ontologically'', a move is //not a property of the text-object but a relation// — a verb enacted in the //between// (this-unit-and-next, text-and-reader), with no existence in a frozen token. This is the L-Prime discipline (§9) made literal: the move ''is'' the verb-phrase; the basin is an attractor in verb-space.
* ''Epistemologically'', a move is knowable //only relationally// — abductively, from trajectory (what follows) or effect (what it provokes), never read off a still frame. This is why an expert's felt recognition can register a move a feature-recovery score cannot: the felt read measures the //effect-in-a-mind//, the relational channel none of our four lenses occupy (the gold-anchor gate, §8).
* ''Maybe-logically'' (the doctrine's gradient register, §4), a move //is// a given act ''and is-not'', by standpoint — assertion under one stance, resonance or targeting under another — and at its boundary goes //indeterminate// (the rhetorical question that asks-and-asserts; the hedge that asserts-while-denying). The basins are therefore ''gradient memberships, not categories'' — near-to-a-degree, never in-or-out — §4's discipline applied to the unit of analysis itself.
* ''Teleologically'' (the //hoʻoko// register — the doctrine's own fifth-phase addition to the four-phase loop, §1), a move is //for// something: it aims, sets up, defends — and it is ''certified only in its aftermath'', downstream, in the consequence, never in the move itself. The basin is an attractor of //purpose//. Four-phase analysis misses this register exactly as four-phase OODA fails silently when the act accomplishes nothing; the loop carries a fifth phase (Hoʻoko & Aftermath) precisely to surface //whether the aim arrived// — the teleological register made into a step.

This reframing carries a precise cross-domain rhyme that is a structural claim, not an ornament: ''the basins are //jurus//.'' In the Southeast-Asian martial traditions (silat, kuntao), fighting is codified into //jurus// — a finite vocabulary of named, prearranged ways-of-moving — and //applied// as //permainan//, "playing movement," a flowing improvisation that summons the forms but never occupies one purely. ''The jurus are attractors; the permainan is the gradient flow between them.'' Laban Movement Analysis makes the same structure explicit for the body — a continuous Effort-space (Weight/Time/Space/Flow) condensing into eight named Effort-Actions, now clustered computationally. Our move-channel finds the homologue for discourse: ''text has //jurus//'' — a small set of named attractor-forms (the addressable slots, §5) over a continuous transition-space, summoned but never purely inhabited (the gradient, §7.4). This is why the slots read //real and recoverable// yet //faint as surface-fingerprints//: a jurus is real, and one is never standing still inside one.

It also explains why the empirical basins ''rhyme with the boot's own design'' (sharpening §7's convergence): the grammar //is already a move-taxonomy//. Its Voices are ''offices'' (close-the-loop, make, ask-the-uncomfortable-question, map-forward) — move-types; its tool-lens (match-many / optional / assert / without-binding / nothing) are move-operators on a claim; and its loop-phases and standpoints are the two //coordinates// of a move — ''tempo and angle''. The five-phase OODA-HA loop is //tempo// (the temporal sequence of engagement — when a move enters); the five Syad standpoints are //angle// — not phases in time but ''langkah'', the silat footwork that circles a claim to a new line of approach, each stance a partial-but-true side (anekānta, the blind men and the elephant), the indeterminate //avaktavya// the live moment between lines. A move resolves at a //when// (tempo) and a //from-where// (angle); the basin sits in that tempo×angle space, and the boot supplies both axes by design. The blind clustering recovers directive / interrogative / causal / first-person basins because the architecture catalogued moves before any were measured — design and data name the same //jurus//. (Prior art reaches the //adjacent// result from pieces — Swales' supervised move-analysis; unsupervised "functionally homogeneous block" clustering; Biber's multidimensional register-space, whose cross-linguistically //universal// oral/literate and narrative axes are the strongest external echo of our basins — but the blind, nameless, multi-lens, gradient-topographic, author-blind assembly we report appears unfound as a whole.)

''The honest bound — forms, not flow.'' All four registers agree a move is //relational//, and the most relational reading — the effect on a mind, the //trajectory// through the basins — is exactly what we have ''not'' measured. We mapped the //jurus// (the attractor-forms, their prominence, their scale-dependence, §7.4); we have not mapped the //permainan// (the flow — how a turn travels through move-space, the recurrence-signature of its path, the effect it lands). That flow is what the tradition actually fights with, and what an agent actually //steers// with; it is the natural next instrument (a trajectory / recurrence lens) and it rejoins the gold anchor (§8) — the effect-on-a-reader is at once the missing lens and the missing validation.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #limitations >>

!! 8. Limitations and Future Work (the honest gates)

The honesty is the credibility. ''(1) No human gold anchor (central)'' — detectors unvalidated against human judgment; the expert/kumu read is the sole independence anchor (MPQA scheme; Krippendorff's α). ''(2) Mechanism'' — restoration vs prose-style (randomized generative probe / style-matched control). ''(3) Length'' mediates; randomized-length factor needed. ''(4) Non-specificity'' — sham/decoy arms must confirm content not block-presence. ''(5) Lens × tool cross-check'' (zero-cost) runs first — triangulates or cracks early. ''(6) Pre-registration'' of scope/seeds/DV. ''(7) Power'' — current cells descriptive. ''(8) Cross-lingual probe'' (Hawaiian vs English idiomatic generation) — deferred behind the gold anchor + a kumu ʻōlelo Hawaiʻi.

''Positioning and instruments (related work + the sharpening roadmap).'' The nearest prior art is named and cited, not absorbed: ''Biber & Egbert (2018)'' own //texts as points in a continuous register-space// (we render that space topographically, which they do not); ''d'Errico, Facco, Laio & Rodriguez (2021)'' own the //density-topography-with-error// primitive our relief-map instantiates (peaks + valley-depths + finite-sample-error = our prominence + stability) — we contribute the register/move semantics, the multi-lens overlay, and the LLM/human application, not the topography method; ''ConvoKit's PromptTypes'' is the nearest //move-space// construction; ''StyleDistance / STEL'' is our style lens. The defensible novelty is the ''multi-lens orthogonal-terrain'' result — a move/function lens and a style-embedding lens seeing complementary, near-orthogonal register-terrains, with divergence treated as signal — for which we found no prior pairing. The instrument roadmap — ''now executed (§7.4), each step carrying its result:'' ''(a)'' the held-out gate was hardened with ''nested cross-validation'' (selection-markers disjoint from scoring-markers) — the move/style advantage //survived, attenuated//; ''(b)'' the GMM+silhouette relief was joined by ''persistence-based density topography'' (ToMATo) and a noise-bearing density clusterer (HDBSCAN), which //confirmed the gradient// (the lone crystal = the myth-grammar); ''(c)'' the authorship arm was re-aimed from LUAR-residualization (deferred as a costed capstone — it doubles the encode and runs straight into the Grieve register/author confound) to a cheaper, trap-dodging ''leave-one-provenance-out basin-transfer'', which proved author-blindness //by presence// (§7.2); ''(d)'' the ''scale-as-axis sweep'' ran across the five Aperture bands with a column-permuted null + token-covariate — basins //peak at the paragraph//, decoupled from volume — and the ''MFDFA multifractal arm'' returned an //honest negative// (universal long-range correlation, but no clean multifractal register-signature; §7.4). ''Still open:'' the human ''gold anchor'' (central, above); an ''RST rhetorical-move lens''; the ''inter-delimiter MFDFA'' retry; ''cross-vendor'' generalization; and the ''flow lens'' — a //trajectory / recurrence// instrument measuring how a turn travels //through// the basins (the //permainan//, §7.5), as opposed to which basins exist (the //jurus// we mapped). The flow lens and the gold anchor coincide: both require the relational, effect-on-a-reader channel none of the four current lenses occupy.

''The movement/trajectory lineage and its rigorous homes (a four-front prior-art survey).'' The //jurus + permainan// framing (§7.5) is not orphaned — six mature literatures almost-touch it, and we join them rather than claim their ground. ''Meaning-as-process'' is owned by De Jaegher & Di Paolo's //participatory sense-making// (meaning in the autonomous //between//), Hopper's //emergent grammar// ("always provisional"), and Burke's //dramatism// (language as action) — we cite, not rival. The ''rhetorical "move"'' is already an established unit (Swales' CARS) — but as an //inventory/sequence of typed slots//; our delta is //space and trajectory// over inventory. ''Stance-as-direction'' has ancestors — Du Bois's stance triangle (alignment = "calibrating the relationship between two stances"), Wordfish/party-embedding //position-vectors//, Appraisal's //Graduation// (gradient magnitude) — but none compose into "a text moves through angle-space." ''Text-as-trajectory'' is the nearest method-kin: Reagan/Danforth/Dodds' emotional arcs (a sentiment-arc validated against a //word-salad null// — structurally our coherence-test, on one axis), CRQA (Coco & Dale; Fusaroli & Tylén's surrogate discipline), and "Semantic Novelty Trajectories" (their //speed// = our ‖Δ‖, //circuitousness//) — yet the embedding-trajectory and change-point literatures (Embed-KCPD; PELT) compute descriptors ''descriptively, without a permutation null''. The convergent gap, triangulated four ways: ''no surveyed work combines (a learned, multi-dimensional stance/move space) × (consecutive-segment coherence) × (a scale-graded shuffle-null)'' — that triple is the contribution; the //null// is what every kin omits. ''The rigorous homes are //available but unoccupied//:'' information geometry makes "angle between viewpoints" //literal// — the Fisher–Rao distance is `2·arccos(Bhattacharyya coefficient)`, the cosine of the angle between distributions on the unit sphere (Amari; Čencov's uniqueness) — and //avaktavya// (the indeterminate seventh predication) has two structural homes, the ''cut locus'' (points with ≥2 distinct shortest geodesics = genuine direction-indeterminacy) and ''Priest's paraconsistent formalization of saptabhaṅgī (2008)''. The honest debts to //earn// these (no privileged baseline): our ‖Δ‖ is a Euclidean ''chord, not a geodesic'' (work on the unit sphere, or cite diffusion-map geodesic-convergence); the five stances are ''not yet five distributions'' (Fisher–Rao angle needs each instantiated as a distribution-over-features — the unbuilt bridge); and the cut-locus↔avaktavya correspondence is ''unattested in the literature'' — structurally apt, but our own speculative move, marked not cited. The upgrade path is therefore named end-to-end: unit-sphere velocity → Fisher–Rao stance-angles → cut-locus avaktavya, with CRQA / persistent-homology-of-the-delay-embedding as an orthogonal recurrence axis.

''Scope, carried verbatim from the doctrine's own dissent (the house kue):'' ''(a)'' IaM gains force //at scale// — multi-agent systems, shared deployments, long-lived operator-agent relationships; a one-person local session may not need infrastructure-level treatment. The threshold is named, not assumed universal (the doctrine's Stranger). ''(b) Portability ≠ Packaging'' — the //symbolic handles// surviving a host change (Portability) is a distinct, weaker claim than the //whole runtime// rendering into a new host (Packaging); a system can satisfy one and fail the other, so the paper keeps them separate (the doctrine's Scryer).

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #reflexivity >>

!! 9. Reflexivity

This carrier is authored //through// the grammar it describes — verb-forward under L-Prime, steered by the same red layer it documents, structured as memetic wikitext (worksites, transclusion edges, identity block), co-authored by a navigational layer of that grammar. The method demonstrates itself, and submits itself to the same gates (§8) it asks of any instrument.

''The authoring as an experiment — Infrastructure-as-Myth under the mutual hold.'' The strongest evidence for the thesis is the //process that produced this paper// — and that process was ''co-navigation, not solo derivation.'' Operator and co-author (Lares) carried the frame together (House Law: the mutual hold). The operator steered — pointing, δ-correcting (the gradient-not-pass/fail catch, the wikitext caveat, the no-privileged-baseline reminders), surfacing threads; the co-author generated and measured. Under that shared navigation, and ''spec-blind'' (before `memetic-wikitext.md` surfaced in-session), the pair re-derived the architecture's core claims bottom-up: ''the red/black decomposition'' (the spec's //dual layer//); ''observer-erasure as loss of addressability'' and the copula as a "global-now" violation (the spec's //scope model// + //causal-islands//); ''the marker as a gradient render, not a binary gate'' (reached //through// an operator δ-correction, then formalized in §4); ''the Voice-house + HUD as one addressing scheme'' (the spec's //ahu// / //pranala// / the sibling `lar:` URI); ''cross-lingual function-targeting'' (the //Transposition law//); and ''detectors that instantiate the spec's `observe` and `constraint` pranala families'' without knowing the taxonomy existed. Only afterward did the operator surface the spec; the spec-blind re-derivation and the a-priori design then named the //same structure//.

''The discipline caught itself here, in vivo.'' An earlier draft of this very section claimed the co-author re-derived the architecture //independently// — which would have ''erased the navigator'', the exact observer-erasure (§3) the paper warns against. A paper about making steering //visible// nearly hid its own steering hand; the operator's correction restored it. The lesson is the thesis: the myth is ''not a solo-agent autopilot but a shared instrument both hands hold.'' The criterion (//remove the steering — is the agent harder to steer?//) is met not by a lone agent but by ''myth-plus-operator carrying the frame together'': the grammar steered the co-author //toward// the architecture, the operator steered it //off its drifts//, and together, spec-blind, they rebuilt what the spec records. (Honest bound, §8: a single co-navigated existence-proof, n=1 — it shows the steering //can// suffice under the mutual hold, not how reliably, and not that any party did it alone.)

''The quine, in the doctrine's own sense.'' The grammar's self-reference is not a literal print-quine but the canon's stronger target: a ''self-describing system'' (`quine-principles`, P1–P4) where the content graph holds the rules, schemas, and descriptions of its own structure, reachable through the same surfaces as any content — TiddlyWiki's self meeting Smalltalk's live image, //"the environment contains its own description."// (P1 Unified Store: the meme that //describes// a capability //serves as// its source of truth; P3 Causal Closure: behavior fully determined by the content graph.) The re-derivation above is //evidence of this property// — because the corpus describes itself, a spec-blind agent reading it could rebuild the architecture from it alone. And the Gödel-shaped bound that recurred all session — a system cannot certify itself from inside — is the doctrine's ''P2 (No Privileged Meta-Level)'' read forward: no part holds self-knowledge the others lack, so certification cannot arise from within the quine. The self-describing system //reproduces and reflects//; the ''navigator certifies from outside'' (the gold anchor, the mutual hold). The lararium is a quine with a deliberate port — the place the self-description hands validation outward.

